{"id":"twitter:2051666372787069397","tweet_id":"2051666372787069397","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051666372787069397","title":"@ZackKorman boundary question for Gov customers. If I have sensitive data I don't want a cloud tool inspecting that data, I need to enforce if the dat","summary":"@ZackKorman boundary question for Gov customers. If I have sensitive data I don't want a cloud tool inspecting that data, I need to enforce if the data is included in prompts and responses with agents. Sounds like if data is in scope for agent, data is in scope for Embroidery Makes sense","date":"2026-05-05","published":"2026-05-05T14:12:36+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/ZackKorman/status/2051658247900131679","reply_tweet_id":"2051658247900131679","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@ZackKorman boundary question for Gov customers. If I have sensitive data I don&#x27;t want a cloud tool inspecting that data, I need to enforce if the data is included in prompts and responses with agents.<br><br>Sounds like if data is in scope for agent, data is in scope for Embroidery<br><br>Makes sense</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051666372787069397","display_date":"May 05, 2026 · 14:12 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
