{"id":"twitter:1913062816812057069","tweet_id":"1913062816812057069","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1913062816812057069","title":"We have a family friend being sued by the IRS for illegally taking Social Security for her dead husband. But he died in 2025, and not 2024. But Social","summary":"We have a family friend being sued by the IRS for illegally taking Social Security for her dead husband. But he died in 2025, and not 2024. But Social Security marked him dead at some point. Now the IRS wants money and there is nobody at Social Security to help.","date":"2025-04-18","published":"2025-04-18T02:51:33+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>We have a family friend being sued by the IRS for illegally taking Social Security for her dead husband.<br><br>But he died in 2025, and not 2024.<br><br>But Social Security marked him dead at some point.<br><br>Now the IRS wants money and there is nobody at Social Security to help.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1913062816812057069","display_date":"April 18, 2025 · 02:51 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
