{"id":"twitter:1912238927013982678","tweet_id":"1912238927013982678","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1912238927013982678","title":"@TheRealRhllor @juha_remes That is why I was asking. I only know the Catholic tradition. There is no Good Friday Mass, just the Station of the Cross s","summary":"@TheRealRhllor @juha_remes That is why I was asking. I only know the Catholic tradition. There is no Good Friday Mass, just the Station of the Cross service. I wondered if the more millineal Protestant wing who hopes for rapture celebrated the crucifixion.","date":"2025-04-15","published":"2025-04-15T20:17:42+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/TheRealRhllor/status/1912237722103669142","reply_tweet_id":"1912237722103669142","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@TheRealRhllor @juha_remes That is why I was asking. I only know the Catholic tradition.<br><br>There is no Good Friday Mass, just the Station of the Cross service.<br><br>I wondered if the more millineal Protestant wing who hopes for rapture celebrated the crucifixion.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1912238927013982678","display_date":"April 15, 2025 · 20:17 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
