{"id":"twitter:2051450241048592588","tweet_id":"2051450241048592588","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051450241048592588","title":"@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Had White House not gone full Orange Jesus, midterms could have all been about choice and reading. (Always bed partners, Phy","summary":"@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Had White House not gone full Orange Jesus, midterms could have all been about choice and reading. (Always bed partners, Phyliss Schafly did phonics lessons at Council for National Policy annual dinners) GOP could have made generational gains in Hispanic and Latin communities","date":"2026-05-04","published":"2026-05-04T23:53:46+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051449306033295697","reply_tweet_id":"2051449306033295697","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Had White House not gone full Orange Jesus, midterms could have all been about choice and reading.<br><br>(Always bed partners, Phyliss Schafly did phonics lessons at Council for National Policy annual dinners)<br><br>GOP could have made generational gains in Hispanic and Latin communities</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051450241048592588","display_date":"May 04, 2026 · 23:53 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2051449306033295697","tweet_id":"2051449306033295697","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051449306033295697","title":"@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Like when you spell connotation wrong. Knowing the Latin bits of con and and the root word help you with knowledge and spell","summary":"@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Like when you spell connotation wrong. Knowing the Latin bits of con and and the root word help you with knowledge and spelling. You can get by at a 6th grade level, even through college. You can also be smart, spend 44 billion on Twitter, and still not get proper editing.","date":"2026-05-04","published":"2026-05-04T23:50:03+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051448455961137503","reply_tweet_id":"2051448455961137503","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Like when you spell connotation wrong. Knowing the Latin bits of con and and the root word help you with knowledge and spelling.<br><br>You can get by at a 6th grade level, even through college.<br><br>You can also be smart, spend 44 billion on Twitter, and still not get proper editing.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051449306033295697","display_date":"May 04, 2026 · 23:50 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2051448455961137503","tweet_id":"2051448455961137503","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051448455961137503","title":"@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Those same states can also have the biggest range in highest scoring and lowest scoring students. (Frank's state is a perfec","summary":"@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Those same states can also have the biggest range in highest scoring and lowest scoring students. (Frank's state is a perfect example). The stats from PIAC (adult literacy) are correct. It's also at \"sixth grade\" where words become derivational in conontation and spelling.","date":"2026-05-04","published":"2026-05-04T23:46:40+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/liberalpuppy/status/2051373415290814835","reply_tweet_id":"2051373415290814835","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@liberalpuppy @FrankLuntz Those same states can also have the biggest range in highest scoring and lowest scoring students.<br><br>(Frank&#x27;s state is a perfect example).<br><br>The stats from PIAC (adult literacy) are correct.<br><br>It&#x27;s also at &quot;sixth grade&quot; where words become derivational in conontation and spelling.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051448455961137503","display_date":"May 04, 2026 · 23:46 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
