{"id":"twitter:2051307950107460058","tweet_id":"2051307950107460058","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051307950107460058","title":"@WhenOnKStreet @Alph4betSoup It's a good study on historical data, the landscape shifted dramatically in 2022 and has only devolved (opinion not empir","summary":"@WhenOnKStreet @Alph4betSoup It's a good study on historical data, the landscape shifted dramatically in 2022 and has only devolved (opinion not empirical data because I have no API to scrape data)","date":"2026-05-04","published":"2026-05-04T14:28:21+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/WhenOnKStreet/status/2051298263848845440","reply_tweet_id":"2051298263848845440","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@WhenOnKStreet @Alph4betSoup It&#x27;s a good study on historical data, the landscape shifted dramatically in 2022  and has only devolved<br><br>(opinion not empirical data because I have no API to scrape data)</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051307950107460058","display_date":"May 04, 2026 · 14:28 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2051307694347218966","tweet_id":"2051307694347218966","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051307694347218966","title":"@d1ngbat_ @Alph4betSoup The data set is only up to 2020 when we still had API access and Twitter still had a safety team Is it still 20% normal flow a","summary":"@d1ngbat_ @Alph4betSoup The data set is only up to 2020 when we still had API access and Twitter still had a safety team Is it still 20% normal flow and 40% during peak times? Not sure. Last study I saw before API was turned off put the estimate of new accounts being bots at around 70%","date":"2026-05-04","published":"2026-05-04T14:27:20+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/d1ngbat_/status/2051300764149076072","reply_tweet_id":"2051300764149076072","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@d1ngbat_ @Alph4betSoup The data set is only up to 2020 when we still had API access and Twitter still had a safety team<br><br>Is it still 20% normal flow and 40% during peak times?<br><br>Not sure. Last study I saw before API was turned off put the estimate of new accounts being bots at around 70%</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051307694347218966","display_date":"May 04, 2026 · 14:27 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2051306463834902817","tweet_id":"2051306463834902817","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2051306463834902817","title":"This seems like an important paper and I can't wait to read. Personally I don't make a distinction between human and npc bots, I don't have the toolse","summary":"This seems like an important paper and I can't wait to read. Personally I don't make a distinction between human and npc bots, I don't have the toolset or time Especially with no API access anymore. Now you have to interact with bots to manually map networks, it sucks https://x.com/Alph4betSoup/status/2051297451651314093","date":"2026-05-04","published":"2026-05-04T14:22:27+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>This seems like an important paper and I can&#x27;t wait to read.<br><br>Personally I don&#x27;t make a distinction between human and npc bots, I don&#x27;t have the toolset or time<br><br>Especially with no API access anymore.<br><br>Now you have to interact with bots to manually map networks, it sucks <a href=\"https://x.com/Alph4betSoup/status/2051297451651314093\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/Alph4betSoup/status/2051297451651314093</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2051306463834902817","display_date":"May 04, 2026 · 14:22 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
